    "biography": "<p>Roland Nazon’s fork posing as a personal assistant</p><p><strong>Morph:</strong> Neotenic</p><p><strong>Motivations:</strong> +Anonymity +Profit +Respect through Fear</p><p><strong>Skills:</strong> Academics: Neuroscience 60, Deception 45 (75), Fray 80, Free Fall 75, Impersonation 45 (75), Infiltration 70, Interest: Underlings' Schemes 80, Interfacing 50, Intimidation 75, Investigation 50, Kinesics 45 (65), Kinetic Weapons 75, Language: English 60, Language: French (Native) 90, Language: Mandarin 60, Networking: Criminal 80, Networking: Hypercorps 45, Networking: Scientists 55, Perception 50, Persuasion 60, Profession: Crime Boss 80, Profession: Identity Theft 80, Programming 40, Psychosurgery 60, Research 40, Unarmed Combat 70</p><p><strong>Implants:</strong> Anti-Glare, Basic Biomods, Basic Mesh Inserts, Bioweave Armor (Light), Cortical Stack, Eelware, Drug Gland (Neem), Emergency Farcaster, Emotional Dampeners, Enhanced Vision, Hardened Skeleton, Medichines, Muscle Augmentation, Neurachem (Level 2), Reflex Booster</p><p><strong>Traits:</strong> Addiction (Major, Neem), Mental Disorder (Megalomania), Trauma Tolerance (Level 2), Social Stigma (Neotenic), Tough (Level 3)</p><p><strong>Gear:</strong> Invisibility Cloak, Personal Interaction Sensor, Security AI, Tactical Network</p><p><strong>ranged:</strong> Submachinegun 75 (85) (AP −2, DV 3d10 + 3, Mode SA/BF/FA, Ammo 20) with ammo Overload, Smartlink</p><p><strong>melee:</strong> Unarmed 70 (AP −2, DV 2d10 + 1 + shock)</p><p><strong>melee:</strong> Injector Nanoswarmwith BTX2,</p><p><strong>Armor:</strong> 10/13 (Second Skin, Smart Fabric Vacsuit)</p><p><strong>Notes:</strong> Counts as a small target (−10 to hit)</p><p><strong>Appearance:</strong> Elleggua appears as a wiry, mixed race boy in flowing red and black clothing.</p><p><strong>Roleplaying:</strong> Elleggua is the “real” Roland Nazon. The neotenic contains the same ruthless sociopath whose calculating brutality turned the Fall into a business opportunity. In many ways, his outlook has never left the squalor of the refugee camps: everyone is an asset to exploit or an example to be made. The same innate understanding of suspicion and fear that launched Lapriyè informs his years of deception. Imitating the servant of an addled king has revealed countless schemes to steal his throne. Elleggua uses Nazon’s veneer of weakness to expose his enemies, then orchestrates their demise before they become a real threat. Even if someone were to succeed in eliminating Nazon, one can’t assassinate a King that doesn’t exist.</p><p><em>Printed: INIT 10, SPD 4, LUC 40, TT 8, IR 80, DUR 50, WT 10, DR 75.</em></p><p><em>Source: Eclipse Phase The Devotees, p. 24.</em></p>",
    "notes": "",
    "details": {
      "motivations": "+Anonymity +Profit +Respect through Fear"
    }
  },
  "items": [
    {
      "_id": "6cee3432ba3e33a9",
      "name": "Neotenic",
      "type": "morph",
      "img": "icons/svg/mystery-man.svg",
      "system": {
        "morphType": "biomorph",
        "aptitudeMax": {
          "cog": 30,
          "coo": 30,
          "int": 30,
          "ref": 30,
          "sav": 30,
          "som": 20,
          "wil": 30
        },
        "aptitudeBonus": {
          "cog": 0,
          "coo": 5,
          "int": 5,
          "ref": 5,
          "sav": 0,
          "som": 0,
          "wil": 0
        },
        "durability": 30,
        "speedMod": 0,
        "initMod": 0,
        "armor": {
          "energy": 0,
          "kinetic": 0
        },
        "movement": "4/20",
        "implants": "Basic Biomods, Basic Mesh Inserts, Cortical Stack",
        "advantages": "+5 COO, +5 INT, +5 REF, +5 to one other aptitude of the player’s choice",
        "disadvantages": "Social Stigma (Neotenic) trait",
        "skillBonuses": [],
        "cpCost": 25,
        "creditCost": "Expensive",
        "active": true,
        "description": "<p>Neotenics are transhumans modified to retain a child-like form. They are smaller, more agile, inquisitive, and less resource-depleting, making them ideal for habitat living and spacecraft. Some people find neotenic sleeves distasteful, especially when employed in certain media and sex work capacities.</p><p><strong>Notes:</strong> Small Size trait</p><p><em>Source: Eclipse Phase Morph Recognition Guide, p. 68.</em></p>"
      },
      "effects": [],
      "flags": {},
